        <div class="story-box">


np: I was in the living room, sitting back on the couch with the TV on. I wasn’t really watching. My thoughts were drifting when my phone suddenly vibrated in my hand. A new message popped up. /np
Unknown: "Hey handsome. Where are you? Can you come to my home?" /en
np: I stared at the screen for a second, then typed back. /np
MC: "Yeah. I can come." /en
np: A moment later, an address appeared. It wasn’t far. I grabbed my jacket and left. /np
np: Twenty minutes later, I stood in front of a quiet house. The lights inside were on. I knocked. The door opened almost immediately. /np
np: She stood there, leaning slightly against the doorframe. Her eyes scanned me slowly, and a faint smile curved her lips. /np
Woman: "You came fast." /en
MC: "You said you needed help." /en
np: She stepped aside, letting me in. The door closed behind me with a soft click. The room was dim, warm, and quiet. /np
np: She turned to face me fully, her expression shifting into something more deliberate. /np
Woman: "I do need help." /en
MC: "With what?" /en
np: She moved closer, reducing the distance between us. /np
Woman: "I heard you’re close to Gatita. And Angie." /en
MC: "I know them." /en
Woman: "Then you’re perfect." /en
np: She paused, watching my reaction. /np
Woman: "I need a diary. Gatita keeps it with her." /en
MC: "A diary?" /en
Woman: "Yes." /en
np: Her tone was calm but loaded with intention. /np
Woman: "If you bring it to me… I’ll return the favor." /en
MC: "Return it how?" /en
np: She smiled again and stepped even closer, her hand brushing lightly against my leg as she leaned in. /np
Woman: "However you want." /en
np: Her fingers lingered just long enough to make her meaning clear. She looked up at me, waiting for my answer. /np











